            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for to lead to, then the Tamil for to affect."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: சாதகம்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சாதகம் — cātakam — \"an advantage\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "இந்தத் திட்டத்தில் பல சாதகங்கள் இருக்கின்றன. intat tiṭṭattil pala cātakaṅkaḷ irukkiṉṟaṉa. This plan has many advantages."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: சாதகங்கள், cātakaṅkaḷ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சாதகமாக, in one's favour. The wind is in our favour: காற்று நமக்குச் சாதகமாக இருக்கிறது."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சாதகம் (cātakam) is borrowed from Sanskrit sādhaka, \"effective, conclusive\" (CDIAL 13333a), from sādh-, \"to succeed\": what helps a thing succeed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
